# Frasma illustration style

Match `public/image/use_case/caso-01-alimentare.jpg`, `caso-02-lamiera.jpg`, `caso-03-cella-frigo.jpg`, and `caso-04-agricoltura.jpg`.

- Technical architectural line drawing: even ink outlines, muted fills (steel, paper white, sage, earth, safety yellow).
- Observational workplace scenes: operators, real machines, factory / warehouse / field. People in workwear, realistic proportions.
- Translate diagrams into scenes (a funnel becomes a bench with incoming documents; a matrix becomes two desks).
- Blog covers and inline figures: 16:9. Pass those four JPGs as `reference_image_paths` on GenerateImage.
- No text, or rare tiny Italian labels only.

Never: cartoon robots or mascots, parchment/sepia paper, infographic flowcharts, English labels, or `public/images/blog/cover-agenti-ai-erp.png` as a style reference.
